{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#lead-childcare-teacher": {
      "title": "Lead Childcare Teacher",
      "description": ". The University of Dubuque offers an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: The Lead Childcare Teacher plays a vital role in creating a nurturing and stimulating learning environment for young children. This position is responsible for planning and implementing developmentally appropriate daily activities aligned with the Creative Curriculum, utilizing diverse teaching techniques to foster children's cognitive, social, emotional, and physical growth. Additionally, this role involves guiding and mentoring assistant teachers and other staff, promoting their professional development, and actively fostering a welcoming, inclusive atmosphere that celebrates diversity and positive social interactions. Primary Responsibilities: Plan daily activities and post weekly lesson plans based on Creative Curriculum, along with utilizing a variety of teaching techniques (storytelling, multi-sensory, games, etc.) to teach children and help them explore their interests Maintain a clean and organized classroom, ensuring the safety of children during all activities and responding appropriately to emergencies Help facilitate daily activities that are developmentally appropriate for the age group, promoting cognitive, social, emotional, and physical development Communicate effectively with parents regarding their child's progress, addressing concerns, and building strong relationships Provide guidance to assistant teachers and other staff members, and helping them develop their skills Promote diversity, positive social interactions and a welcoming atmosphere for all children Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Position Skills and Abilities: Effective communication with children, parents, and coworkers Ability to work with young children and understand their needs Ability to multi task and prioritize multiple responsibilities Ability to work collaboratively with other staff members, including assistants, building strong teamwork, along with a cohesive and supportive learning environment Ability to bend, lift up to 50 lbs., stoop, kneel, and be on your feet for extended periods of time Work with children from diverse backgrounds and culture Requirements: Associate Degree Required; Graduate Degree Preferred Current certification in First Aid, CPR, Universal Precautions, and Mandatory Reporting training is preferred: ability to obtain certifications after employment is required Previous experience working with children is required Ability to work a flexible schedule is preferred Excellent communication skills - verbal, written, and interpersonal To apply with a growing faith-based University for the"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#social-media-specialist": {
      "title": "Social Media Specialist",
      "description": "position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/ Admission Counselor Toggle Accordion Visibility The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking an"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#admission-counselor": {
      "title": "Admission Counselor",
      "description": "in the Office of Admission.  The University of Dubuque offers an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: The Admission Counselor is responsible for executing strategic undergraduate recruitment efforts within an assigned geographic territory. This position represents the University of Dubuque at high schools, college fairs, community events, and campus programs, while providing individualized admission counseling to prospective students and families. The Admission Counselor collaborates with admission leadership to develop territory-specific recruitment strategies, evaluate applications, analyze enrollment data, and contribute to achieving institutional enrollment goals. Primary Responsibilities: Manage all recruitment activities within assigned geographic territory to support undergraduate enrollment goals Provide admission counseling to prospective students, parents, and school counselors regarding admission policies, procedures, academic programs, and financial aid opportunities Represent the University of Dubuque at college fairs, high school visits, receptions, and on-campus recruitment events Collaborate with the Associate Dean of Admission to develop and implement a strategic territory recruitment plan and travel schedule Evaluate admission applications and analyze enrollment funnel data to monitor recruitment progress and improve student conversion outcomes Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Position Skills and Abilities: Strong verbal and written communication skills with the ability to effectively present information to diverse audiences Ability to build and maintain positive relationships with students, families, school counselors, and campus partners Strong organizational, planning, and time-management skills with attention to detail Ability to work independently while contributing effectively as a member of a collaborative team Proficiency in utilizing data and enrollment management systems to support recruitment strategies and decision-making Requirements: Undergraduate Degree Required in Business Administration, Marketing, Communications, or a related field; Graduate Degree preferred Previous experience in college admission, recruitment, sales, marketing, or a related field preferred Ability to travel extensively and transport admission materials, displays, and equipment; valid driver's license required Demonstrate ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds and cultures Ability to work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends, and perform event-related activities that may require extended standing, walking, and climbing stairs To apply with a growing faith-based University for the"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#student-accounts-collection-coordinator": {
      "title": "Student Accounts Collection Coordinator",
      "description": ".  The University of Dubuque offers an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: The Student Accounts Collection Coordinator is a member of the Student Accounts team with primary responsibility for managing delinquent receivables. This position ensures the timely generation of account statements and coordinates effective collection efforts while providing exceptional customer service to students, families, faculty, staff, and external partners. Primary Responsibilities: Generate and distribute billing for student accounts and institutional loans Counsel students and families regarding billing statements, payment options, and account discrepancies, and establish payment plans in accordance with university policy Determine and process account write-offs in compliance with university policy and applicable regulations Credit report delinquent accounts to credit bureaus Ensure compliance with federal, state, and institutional regulations related to debt collection Review accounts with outstanding balances to determine transcript eligibility Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Skills and Abilities: Strong interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills Excellent knowledge of Microsoft products (Excel, Word, etc.) Ability to use discretion and confidentiality in accordance with FERPA and University matters Ability to work independently and collaboratively Strong understanding of receivables management and credit bureau reporting Ability to remain seated at a workstation for extended periods of time Strong organizational, time management, and problem-solving abilities Qualifications: Associate Degree Required; Undergraduate Degree Preferred 2-4 years of experience with accounts receivable with specific focus on credit reporting To apply with a growing faith-based University for the"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#enterprise-application-data-services-specialist": {
      "title": "Enterprise Application & Data Services Specialist",
      "description": ". The University of Dubuque offers a competitive wage and an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: The Enterprise Application and Data Services Specialist will play a key role in helping the University of Dubuque to optimize data quality and workflow processes, assist with system integrations, and improve reporting and analytical support. This role will collaborate closely with and support individuals and departments across campus to strengthen our use of technical systems and improve efficiencies related to technology, data and processes. Primary Responsibilities: Identify, develop and correct procedures for monitoring accuracy and quality of data Work with stakeholders to educate, assist and update data and processes Write and maintain stored procedures and functions to extract, transform and report on data Provide recommendations and technical expertise regarding the use of all University systems and the data within said systems Design, develop and generate reports to meet the needs of users across campus in a timely, efficient and accurate manner Provide data-driven insights by collecting, analyzing and reporting on trends to support strategic decision making Create forms and workflows to assist in improving processes and data flow between and within departments across campus Automate processes to allow faculty and staff to spend more time interacting with students versus performing arduous tasks and unneeded paperwork Be a partner that others across campus can rely upon to provide high-quality assistance and insight regarding needs related to systems, data and processes Understand proper integration and documentation of the use of all software tools used to manage the University of Dubuque's data Keep abreast of upgrades to all systems and how these will help deliver the best data and most efficient process improvement to end users Research and have knowledge of new technologies as well as investigate unused modules of current systems as potential ways to improve processes Document all procedures so they can be understood and supported by other team members as well as end users Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's mission Position Skills and Abilities: Strong technical aptitude Proficient in problem-solving project management and analytical skills Strong understanding of process improvement and workflow development Ability to manage several high-priority projects simultaneously while producing quality work in a timely and accurate manner Excellent communication and collaboration skills Ability to develop, build and strengthen relationships to create partnerships with stakeholders from all areas of the university Strong attention to detail Ability to investigate and understand processes to deliver timely, accurate and actionable solutions Strong problem solving and analytical skills Self-motivated and highly responsible Ability to work alone as well as collaborate with others Requirements: Undergraduate Degree Required; Computer emphasis preferred or related business experience Experience using report writers, preferably SQL Server Reporting Services and Power BI Strong understanding and experience of relational database applications Experience with TSQL in developing SQL scripts, procedures and functions To apply with a growing faith-based University for the"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#enterprise-systems-integration-analyst-programmer": {
      "title": "Enterprise Systems Integration Analyst/Programmer",
      "description": ". The University of Dubuque offers a competitive wage and an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: The Enterprise Systems Integration Analyst/Programmer will play a critical role in supporting, enhancing, and integrating the University of Dubuque's enterprise systems. This position focuses on systems analysis, data integration, automation, and technical problem solving to improve data flow, system reliability, and user experience across campus. The role collaborates closely with functional departments to understand business needs and translates them into scalable, maintainable technical solutions that support the University's mission. Primary Responsibilities: Collaborate with stakeholders across campus to understand business processes, data needs and system challenges Analyze existing systems and workflows and recommend technical or process improvements! Translate functional requirements into technical designs and specifications Develop, maintain, and enhance scripts, procedures, and automation to support institutional systems and workflows Utilize scripting and programming languages (e.g., Python, JavaScript, T-SQL) to support data processing, integration and automation Ensure code quality, documentation and adherence to best practices Create forms and workflows to assist in improving processes and data flow between and within departments across campus Automate processes to allow faculty and staff to spend more time interacting with students versus performing arduous tasks and unneeded paperwork Be a partner that others across campus can rely upon to provide high-quality assistance and insight regarding needs related to systems, data and processes Design, implement, and support integrations between systems using APIs, data feeds and other integration methods Monitor and troubleshoot integrations to ensure data accuracy, reliability and performance Collaborate with vendors and internal teams on system upgrades, patches and integration changes Support and enhance web-based applications, forms and campus portal functionality Assist with the configuration and scripting of user-facing systems to improve usability, accessibility, and overall user experience Work collaboratively with stakeholders to identify opportunities to better leverage existing web platforms Support reporting and analytics initiatives by ensuring reliable data availability and integration Assist in the development of reports, dashboards and data extracts used for operational and strategic decision-making Serve as a secondary support resource for key enterprise applications, learning system configurations, scripting, and workflows as needed to ensure continuity of operations Document system logic, integrations, procedures and technical configurations so they can be supported by others Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's mission Position Skills and Abilities: Strong analytical, problem-solving, and technical aptitude Ability to manage multiple priorities while producing accurate, high-quality work Excellent communication and collaboration skills, including the ability to work effectively with both technical and non-technical stakeholders Ability to investigate and understand business processes to deliver effective technical solutions Strong attention to detail and commitment to documentation and maintainability Self-motivated, adaptable, and highly responsible Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively within a team environment Experience collaborating with functional users to improve processes through technology Requirements: Undergraduate Degree Required; bachelor's degree in computer science, Information Systems, Software Engineering, or a related field preferred, or equivalent professional experience Familiar with workflow automation, forms platforms, or document management solutions Experience working with relational databases and SQL-based systems Experience with scripting or programming languages such as Python and JavaScript Familiar with API-based integrations and data exchange concepts Experience in supporting or developing web-based systems or applications Experience working in a higher education or similarly complex, multi-system environment Experience supporting or integrating enterprise systems such as student information systems, document management systems, learning management systems or campus portals To apply with a growing faith-based University for the"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#physician-assistant": {
      "title": "Physician Assistant",
      "description": "at the Smeltzer-Kelly Student Health Center. Position Summary: The Physician Associate (Assistant) at the University of Dubuque's Smeltzer-Kelly Student Health Center provides comprehensive, student-centered primary and acute healthcare services, including assessment, diagnosis, treatment, follow-up care, ordering and interpreting diagnostic tests, prescribing medications, and performing select procedures. Working independently and collaboratively within an interdisciplinary team, this role develops individualized care plans while promoting wellness, disease prevention, and health education through a holistic approach that supports students' physical, mental, and emotional well-being. The Physician Associate (Assistant) also partners with campus departments to coordinate care, contributes to health promotion and preventive health initiatives, and fosters a welcoming, inclusive, and confidential environment that supports student success and a healthy campus community. Primary Responsibilities: Perform direct patient care for University of Dubuque students including diagnostic and therapeutic services at the Smeltzer-Kelly Student Health Center Function independently and/or as a member of an interdisciplinary team to plan, deliver, and evaluate healthcare for University of Dubuque's student population Promote and support health maintenance, disease prevention and wellness strategies across the continuum of care Perform medical diagnostic and therapeutic procedures, prescribe, dispense or deliver medications in accordance with state and federal scope of practice laws Document all aspects of patient care accurately in the electronic medical record (EMR) and ensure compliance with billing, regulatory and institutional standards Initiate and coordinate referrals to specialists, external providers or other campus services as appropriate for continued care Contribute to the ongoing achievement of Student Health Center goals through active participation in program development, quality improvement and student health initiatives Maintain current clinical competencies and professional expertise through continuing medical education, certifications and best practices Maintain excellent verbal and written communication skills for effective patient education, care coordination and documentation Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's mission Skills and Abilities: Demonstrate excellent interpersonal skills, organizational skills, effective oral and written correspondence and public relations skills Commitment to the mission of the University Ability to prioritize tasks Ability to work both independently and collaboratively as part of an interdisciplinary healthcare team Qualifications: Master's or doctoral degree from an accredited Physician Assistant (Physician Associate) program Current certification by the National Commission on Certification of Physician Assistants (NCCPA) and eligibility for Iowa licensure required Prior experience working with young adult population is preferred To apply with a growing faith-based University for the"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#security-officer": {
      "title": "Security Officer",
      "description": "(Full-time, 3 rd shift).  The University of Dubuque offers an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: The Security Guard is responsible for maintaining a safe and secure environment for all students, faculty, staff, and visitors on campus. This role involves regular foot patrols of university grounds and buildings, enforcing university policies, responding to emergencies, and documenting incidents with accuracy and attention to detail. Security Guards are also tasked with opening and closing campus facilities, issuing parking violations, and operating a multi-line phone and radio dispatch system to coordinate responses effectively.  Security Guards play a critical role in supporting the Mission of the university by ensuring a secure and welcoming campus environment. Primary Responsibilities: Open and close campus facilities Issue parking violations Maintain security and safety of people and property on campus by patrolling on foot Enforce policies in support of the University's mission Answer emergency and non-emergency calls and document important information Respond to any issues and follow-up by coordinating with the appropriate departments or officers Operate and manage a multi-line telephone system Use the radio, phone, or computer to direct officers to the appropriate sites Prioritize and organize calls according to urgency Maintain and update call logs, call records and other important documentation Update requests for access from various departments through the controlled access program Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Skills and Abilities: Familiar with reporting requirements of the Clery Act for Higher Education Must be detail orientated and accurate Ability to walk and climb stairs Knowledge of basic security and fire inspection procedures Quick decision-making skills Excellent verbal and written communication skills Ability to multi-task and work under pressure May be required to walk or stand for extended periods of time May be required to work outdoors in inclement weather May be required to lift, push or pull up to 50 lbs. Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent Valid driver's license Basic computer knowledge Ability to read and comprehend basic written and verbal instructions This position will require night and weekend work. (2nd shift $0.50 shift differential and 3rd shift $0.65 shift differential) To apply with a growing faith-based University for the"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#assistant-women-s-wrestling-coach": {
      "title": "Assistant Women's Wrestling Coach",
      "description": ".  The University of Dubuque offers an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: Reporting to the Head Coach, the Assistant Women's Wrestling Coach assists in developing and implementing a strategic plan for the Athletic and Recreation departments that is consistent with the University Mission and strategic plan, as well as the Student Success Commitment.  This position assists in program development related to student-athlete success and experiences, sport program evaluation and assessment, and effectively engaging the campus and community in athletic events and facilitating experiences within both for student-athletes. Additionally, this position assists in meeting all compliance and eligibility requirements for the University, the American Rivers Conference, and the NCAA; and promoting the safety and well-being of all student-athletes. Finally, this position will have additional duties within the Academic Support Center that promote student success within the classroom and promotes the retention and persistence of student athletes. Primary Responsibilities: Assist in practice planning, execution and on-mat instruction Assist in the collaboration with campus partners and athletic administration regarding facility use, upkeep, and resource management Assist in developing and implementing competition plans, reports, strategies and on-mat duties as assigned Assist in all phases of the recruiting process, specifically the scouting and evaluation of skilled and academically qualified student-athletes, the matriculation process of student-athletes (including application, financial aid completion, housing registration, required paperwork, course registration, and orientation attendance), and collaboration with campus partners regarding the communication processes required Assist in monitoring academic progress of program athletes and serve as a program liaison for staff and faculty and facilitate the utilization of resources to promote student success Collaborate with campus partners and athletic department staff regarding the safety and well-being of student athletes Assist in event management and game promotion/partnerships Assist in camps, clinics, and workshops facilitated by sport program Assist in effectively managing and reporting conduct related incidences within sport program Live and model the UD Mission and engage the campus and surrounding communities in a manner that allows for the retention and persistence of UD students Facilitate educational opportunities and compliance to all University, ARC, and NCAA rules and regulations Serve as a Title IX Campus Security Authority Willingness and ability to be an active participant in following applicable safety rules and regulations, including necessary training and drills Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Skills and Abilities: Strong active listening and effective communication skills Strong social emotional skills and a student-centered approach to teaching and learning Clear capacity for effective conflict resolution and mediation High ethical standards Strong technological skill set Ability to effectively work in a team environment Qualifications: Undergraduate Degree Required; Graduate Degree Preferred Collegiate wrestling experience preferred Previous coaching experience of at least 2 years; preferably at the college level Competency and knowledge related to NCAA rules, policy, and procedures; or experience related to rules and regulations associated with athletics Experience preparing, monitoring, and maintaining budget Appreciation for and ability to work within a collaborative campus community and the ability to assist in building collaborative alliances to serve students and the campus communities To apply with a growing faith-based University for the"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#aviation-maintenance-office-assistant": {
      "title": "Aviation Maintenance Office Assistant",
      "description": ".  The University of Dubuque offers an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: This position will directly support the Director of Aviation Maintenance. Duties include supervised management of the University of Dubuque aircraft fleet for the maintenance director, maintaining the aircraft overhaul slope on a daily basis, coordinating maintenance activities internally and externally through phone and email communications, monitoring aviation parts lists and stockage for use in daily maintenance activities, monitoring MSDS sheets to include storage of chemicals in the hangars, and keeping the director of maintenance informed of all aircraft maintenance issues and recommending maintenance activities. Works with dispatch in keeping an accurate, up-to-date list of flyable and non-flyable aircraft and where they are parked on the ramp, advise on when aircraft become available for use, and place aircraft back into service upon completion of maintenance. Will assist the maintenance director with other duties as required in support of aviation maintenance activities. Primary Responsibilities: Complete daily maintenance overhaul slope updates and advise director of pending overhauls Manage and coordinate flow of aircraft maintenance repairs Track, order and manage inventory for aircraft parts, consumables, and shop supplies Perform standard office duties such as filing, typing, answering phones, and distributing mail Update and manage aircraft maintenance databases and records to ensure compliance and accuracy Maintain accurate logs for aircraft maintenance activities, costs, and compliance for management and regulatory authorities Maintain current hazardous material data sheets and OHSA compliance requirements Coordinate internal and external maintenance activities for aircraft Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Skills and Abilities: Demonstrate proficiency in Microsoft Office, especially Excel and Word, with the ability to manage complex data sheets and create well-formatted documents Strong interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills Ability to prioritize daily and special projects Ability to manage office activities Ability to lift 50 pounds Ability to remain seated at a workstation for extended periods of time Qualifications: Diploma Required; Associate Degree Preferred Office management experience Microsoft Office programs skills Mechanical aptitude preferred Current Schedule: 6:00 am - 2 pm or 7:30 am - 3:30 pm To apply with a growing faith-based University for the"
    },
