positive, respectful, and inclusive learning environment Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with a passion for medical education Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with faculty, staff, and clinical partners Maintain professional and collegial behavior Minimum Qualifications: BSN required; MSN preferred Current unencumbered Iowa Nursing license Experience teaching, precepting, or mentoring students in a clinical or academic setting Knowledge of, and commitment to, the university's philosophy, mission and core values This position is part of an ongoing talent pool. Qualified candidates may be contacted when openings become available. To apply with a growing faith-based University for the"
